00:34:30.480 --> 00:34:50.860
It might be a bean. Don't let your guard down.

00:34:51.020 --> 00:34:51.180
What?

00:35:00.090 --> 00:35:00.470
You?

00:35:01.560 --> 00:35:05.780
I didn't know there was such a beautiful lover.

00:35:06.840 --> 00:35:09.780
As expected of the big artist of the future.

00:35:09.920 --> 00:35:10.770
You're good.

00:35:11.350 --> 00:35:15.320
You guys look good too.

00:35:15.520 --> 00:35:17.870
No, no, this is different.

00:35:18.660 --> 00:35:19.680
It's pretty bad.

00:35:20.120 --> 00:35:20.600
Right?

00:35:21.220 --> 00:35:22.570
I'm used to it.

00:35:22.970 --> 00:35:23.170
Sugar.

00:35:31.210 --> 00:35:33.400
By the way, Oliver, where did you get that score?

00:35:34.260 --> 00:35:36.400
It was in my grandpa's drawer.

00:35:37.340 --> 00:35:38.460
Where is your grandpa?

00:35:39.520 --> 00:35:42.200
Where? Probably in heaven.

00:35:43.240 --> 00:35:47.690
Besides, it's probably in any house around here.

00:35:48.130 --> 00:35:49.220
What did you say?

00:35:50.010 --> 00:35:53.060
Old people sometimes gather there and sing.

00:35:53.800 --> 00:35:57.290
I don't know why or who, but...

00:36:02.040 --> 00:36:08.300
The old people may not know what kind of song it is, but they are singing the song of that score.

00:36:08.660 --> 00:36:14.630
The fragments of memories that we encounter from time to time make us think of unnecessary things.

00:36:14.810 --> 00:36:24.000
If you want to feel happiness in this city, don't resist the memories that appear.

00:36:24.440 --> 00:36:27.000
Roger Smith's Law

00:36:31.470 --> 00:36:34.050
Why don't you buy this? It's beautiful, isn't it?

00:36:34.270 --> 00:36:36.820
But it doesn't mean anything to Lola.

00:36:36.980 --> 00:36:42.210
You can use the chance yourself, if you're an artist.

00:36:46.850 --> 00:36:49.120
Dorothy, do you think Oliver has talent?

00:36:50.020 --> 00:36:50.990
I don't think it's about Saks.

00:36:55.670 --> 00:36:56.190
Youth.

00:36:57.250 --> 00:36:59.250
It's about looking at reality.

00:37:00.090 --> 00:37:01.570
To push through with all your might.

00:37:01.850 --> 00:37:04.040
What's that?

00:37:05.270 --> 00:37:06.530
Roger Smith's Law.

00:37:06.930 --> 00:37:08.040
That's the second one.

00:37:08.160 --> 00:37:17.720
It's a tragic one.

00:37:18.080 --> 00:37:20.730
The day when the crisis will come to Paradigm City.

00:37:20.950 --> 00:37:22.060
To celebrate with everyone.

00:37:22.360 --> 00:37:24.600
There's still no clue.

00:37:26.240 --> 00:37:28.480
After all, that message is just a mockery.

00:37:32.360 --> 00:37:32.680
Hello.

00:37:33.140 --> 00:37:34.900
You are...

00:37:34.900 --> 00:37:36.480
Please tell me.

00:37:37.230 --> 00:37:38.990
Tell you?

00:37:39.270 --> 00:37:54.020
Can I have some tea?

00:37:54.340 --> 00:37:55.360
Just a little.

00:37:55.640 --> 00:37:57.010
But I don't need it.

00:37:57.210 --> 00:37:58.950
I don't know what it tastes like anyway.

00:38:02.880 --> 00:38:03.980
What do you want me to tell you?

00:38:05.570 --> 00:38:07.530
Why does Oliver like you?

00:38:07.810 --> 00:38:11.740
You have feelings that make people like you.

00:38:12.220 --> 00:38:16.270
I'm sorry.

00:38:16.590 --> 00:38:17.520
It's okay.

00:38:17.720 --> 00:38:24.210
Oliver likes me because it's easy to lie to me.

00:38:24.590 --> 00:38:27.200
Oliver has a lot of lies.

00:38:27.860 --> 00:38:29.650
That's fine.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:33.380
He's lying, so he can continue to play saxophone.

00:38:34.320 --> 00:38:44.420
He lives the way he likes, so Oliver and I can do it well.

00:38:45.080 --> 00:38:46.470
That's fine.

00:38:46.770 --> 00:38:50.700
What's that?

00:38:51.100 --> 00:38:52.530
A present.

00:38:52.890 --> 00:38:55.970
But if he doesn't give it to me, it'll be hard for me.

00:39:25.150 --> 00:39:25.490
It took off!

00:39:32.560 --> 00:39:32.760
You

00:40:07.020 --> 00:40:07.140
He won't do anything!

00:40:45.320 --> 00:40:47.460
I won't let a monster like you like this town!

00:40:48.600 --> 00:40:54.590
Megadeus...

00:41:18.080 --> 00:41:20.820
I'm sorry to bother you at a time like this, but can you go get the coat from the tailor?

00:41:22.040 --> 00:41:25.250
I won't be able to make it in time if something happens to Manichi.

00:41:30.440 --> 00:41:30.640
Okay.

00:42:00.830 --> 00:42:01.190
There's no end.

00:42:46.220 --> 00:42:46.360
Bad attitude

00:43:08.410 --> 00:43:09.110
The growth has stopped?

00:43:09.490 --> 00:43:17.480
It was made so that only this much could be lived.

00:43:22.740 --> 00:43:24.380
It doesn't seem like it will cause any harm anymore.

00:43:34.380 --> 00:43:35.080
This place is dangerous.

00:43:35.660 --> 00:43:38.080
Until we get rid of that monster, we'll have to evacuate for now.

00:43:38.480 --> 00:43:47.050
Do you know the true meaning of Heaven's Day?

00:43:48.390 --> 00:43:49.660
The true meaning?

00:43:50.040 --> 00:43:53.640
It's the day when the God's Miko was born.

00:43:54.260 --> 00:43:56.650
Asusui, I'm coming!

00:44:01.080 --> 00:44:01.460
Oliver...

00:44:01.460 --> 00:44:04.700
Lola? Why are you in such a dangerous place?

00:44:05.060 --> 00:44:09.160
I was worried about you.

00:44:09.240 --> 00:44:11.140
Lola...

00:44:11.140 --> 00:44:18.200
Sorry, I couldn't get you a present.

00:44:19.580 --> 00:44:22.780
It's okay. Just stay by my side.

00:44:38.700 --> 00:44:39.260
What's up, Smith?

00:44:39.580 --> 00:44:44.490
I'm going to do something that's not even in style, so I'll ask you for a song.

00:44:45.160 --> 00:44:46.600
Then, I'll take it.

00:44:46.940 --> 00:44:54.790
Dorothy, happy birthday.

00:44:56.420 --> 00:44:59.340
My birthday is the same as Dorothy's real birthday.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:01.240
It's still a long way to go.

00:45:01.300 --> 00:45:03.740
What? Norman!

00:45:06.050 --> 00:45:06.150
Huh?

00:45:06.310 --> 00:45:13.270
It's a gift from Heaven's Day, Roger.

00:45:14.060 --> 00:45:15.880
Dorothy, I...

00:45:15.880 --> 00:45:18.580
Roger, I want to give a gift to someone I'm grateful to.

00:45:20.140 --> 00:45:21.870
I want to do the same as everyone else.

00:45:22.530 --> 00:45:23.910
Dorothy...

00:45:23.910 --> 00:45:27.430
This is from me.

00:45:30.000 --> 00:45:30.660
Thank you, Roger.

00:45:30.920 --> 00:45:45.910
Oliver, this is the best you can do.

00:45:46.500 --> 00:45:47.950
It's a great present.

00:46:36.520 --> 00:46:59.780
It's me that you're the one that

00:47:01.720 --> 00:47:08.080
Only one boss this time amongst the real

00:47:08.080 --> 00:47:16.630
Never felt that love is so worth

00:47:17.230 --> 00:47:23.470
But you're there, someone we could keep

00:47:30.410 --> 00:47:33.170
We'll be together now and home.

00:47:46.070 --> 00:47:46.410
Another.

00:48:52.810 --> 00:48:53.210
Hand over the Gundam!
